meta {
  name: Report - Audit Activity
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/{{realm_id}}/reports/AuditActivity?start_date=2026-03-01&end_date=2026-12-31
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  start_date: 2026-03-01
  end_date: 2026-12-31
  : 
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

docs {
  Fetch the QBO audit log for a date range.
  Returns who created/modified each entity, their email, entity type,
  entity ID, and timestamp — the data source for qbo_created_by.
  
  Response format: columnar report (Header/Columns/Rows) not entity JSON.
  Columns typically include: Date, UserName, EventType, EntityType,
  EntityId, EntityName.
  
  Use this to investigate the SELF_APPROVAL_LOOP graph detection —
  match UserName/email against employees table to find terminated users
  still active in QBO.

  CONFIRMED 2026-07-09 (sandbox realm 9341456594594180): this report
  returns "Permission Denied Error" (code 5020, element ReportName) even
  with a valid access_token carrying com.intuit.quickbooks.accounting
  scope — AuditActivity is gated to QBO Company Admins specifically, not
  just accounting-scope API access. This is NOT what Foundry's sync uses
  and should not be treated as "the primary way" to get user identity —
  syncCreatedBy (internal/datasource/quickbooks/sync.go) deliberately
  uses the TransactionList report's create_by/last_mod_by columns
  instead, which work under normal accounting-scope access without
  requiring the connecting QBO user to be a Company Admin. See
  reports/transaction-list-created-by.bru for the report Foundry
  actually relies on.
}
